**INDIE FILM STARS ALIGN AT SUNDANCE: A RECORD-BREAKING NUMBER OF WELL-KNOWN DIRECTORS BRING NEW WORK TO THE FESTIVAL**

Park City, UT - The Sundance Film Festival, one of the most prestigious and highly anticipated events in the film industry, is gearing up for its 2023 edition, and this year's lineup promises to be one for the books. For the first time in its history, a record-breaking number of well-known indie filmmakers will be bringing their latest projects to the festival, showcasing a diverse range of stories, styles, and genres.

The list of participating directors includes some of the most respected and celebrated names in independent cinema, with a combined total of 15 Oscar nominations and 5 wins between them. The group includes:

* Greta Gerwig (Lady Bird, Little Women), who will premiere her highly anticipated new drama, "The Bells of St. Mary's";
* Barry Jenkins (Moonlight, If Beale Street Could Talk), who will unveil his latest feature, "The Last Black Man in San Francisco";
* Kelly Reichardt (Certain Women, First Cow), who will showcase her latest exploration of the American West, "The River's Edge";
* Alex Ross Perry (Listen Up Philip, Her Smell), who will premiere his new drama, "The Great Pretenders";
* and Miranda July (Me and You and Everyone We Know, The Future), who will debut her latest experimental feature, "The Book of Questions".

"We're thrilled to have such an incredible lineup of talented filmmakers joining us at Sundance this year," said Sundance Film Festival Director, Tabitha Jackson. "Their work is a testament to the power of independent storytelling and the impact it can have on audiences and the industry as a whole."

The festival, which runs from January 19-29, will feature over 120 feature films, including narrative and documentary features, as well as short films and episodic content. The Sundance Film Festival is known for its commitment to showcasing innovative and daring storytelling, and this year's lineup promises to be no exception.

In addition to the impressive list of participating directors, the festival will also feature a number of special events and panels, including a tribute to the pioneering work of indie film icon, John Cassavetes, and a conversation with acclaimed actress, Laura Dern, about her work in independent cinema.

The Sundance Film Festival is a premier platform for independent filmmakers to showcase their work and connect with audiences, industry professionals, and critics. With its rich history of launching the careers of some of the most influential filmmakers of our time, the festival continues to be a must-attend event for anyone passionate about independent cinema.

Tickets for the Sundance Film Festival go on sale December 1, and more information about the festival and its lineup can be found on the official Sundance website.
